, and upside calls aren't unusually cheap.\n- **History:** The IV series runs 24% in 2024, 26% in 2025 and 27% in 2026. It has drifted up slightly but not spiked.\n\nPricing alone gives no edge in either direction. Whether to add depends on your view of VLTX's fundamentals, not on the option prices.\n\nOne related fact for that view: utilities make up 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham Power is 35% of utility orders and Norvane is 21%, so the business is concentrated in a few customers. The other nodes are looking at utility financing and demand.\n\nI only had IV level, median and skew. I had no data on the underlying price, strikes, premiums or the IV percentile, so I haven't compared specific contracts.\n\nSources: `vltx-leaps` doc and the `vltx_iv_history` series (n4.d3).","ttft_ms":1966,"type":"result","duration_ms":23622,"uuid":"4d0a3457-6f94-40de-a8e8-7d3ea8261024","ttft_stream_ms":1015,"time_to_request_ms":117,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":6,"client_creation":4,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":65,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":64,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":187,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":112,"process_rss_mib_result":199,"process_anon_mib_result":117,"process_peak_rss_mib":199,"process_cpu_ms_turn":534,"process_wall_ms_turn":23620,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":50,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1378,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_count":134,"main_stream_chunk_count":14,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":50,"wall_ms":1378,"entries":3},"tool":{"